# ── Expo / React Native (apps/insolvia_app) ─────────────────────
# Expo's local cache: the dev server's resolved config, Metro's transform
# cache, and the generated web `.expo/types`. Regenerated on every `expo
# start`, never committed.
.expo/
# `expo export` output. Anchored per app for the same reason the Node build
# output below is: a bare `dist/` would silently swallow any future build
# directory anywhere in the repo.
/apps/insolvia_app/dist/

# GENERATED, NOT ABSENT. `ios/` and `android/` are the native projects `expo
# prebuild` writes from app.json — the Continuous Native Generation workflow
# (https://docs.expo.dev/workflow/continuous-native-generation/). They are
# build output derived from committed config, so committing them would mean
# hand-maintaining two copies of every native setting and resolving prebuild's
# diffs by hand forever.
#
# There is nothing to ignore today: the app is a web SPA and no prebuild has
# run (see the Xcode/CocoaPods note in scripts/dev-setup.sh). These lines are
# here so that the day mobile starts, a `git add -A` cannot sweep 40 MB of
# generated Xcode/Gradle project into a commit before anyone notices.
/apps/insolvia_app/ios/
/apps/insolvia_app/android/

*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/
coverage/
*.log

# ── Terraform ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfvars                # real vars are secret; *.tfvars.example IS committed
!*.tfvars.example
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
# .terraform.lock.hcl intentionally ignored for now (locks were generated with
# -backend=false during bootstrap). Commit proper multi-platform locks later:
#   terraform providers lock -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=darwin_arm64
.terraform.lock.hcl
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
# Lambda zips built by archive_file at plan time.
infra/modules/*/.build/

# Per-machine local wiring written by scripts/dev-aws-setup.sh (table name,
# profile name — no secrets, but machine-specific and never committed).
/services/api/.env

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── Node (the npm workspace + the version-gated React packages) ─
# package-lock.json IS committed (reproducible npm installs in CI).
node_modules/
storybook-static/
# Build output is anchored per package rather than a bare `dist/`, which would
# silently swallow any future build directory anywhere in the repo. Each new
# Node package that builds adds its own line. (The design system deliberately
# has none: it publishes source — a package-side build would collapse its
# .web/.native leaf pairs.)

# Tool-run artifacts that may sit on disk while a branch that does not track
# their package is checked out (the per-app .gitignore only exists on branches
# where the app does). Ignoring them at the root keeps a `git add -A` from a
# different branch from sweeping them into an unrelated commit.
.lighthouseci/
.react-router/
# Left over from the Flutter era. Nothing in this repo produces it any more,
# but every machine that ever ran the old toolchain still has one on disk, and
# checking out a pre-cutover commit recreates it. Delete this line once no
# working copy has one.
.dart_tool/

# ── OS / editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
